			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Bump devDependencies and synchronize both submodules\n\nUpdate Land's root package.json devDependencies and advance the Dependency and Element submodules to their latest commits, pulling in tooling refinements and the expanded IPC surface.\n\n**package.json:** Bump prettier-plugin-java to 2.9.2 and turbo to 2.9.14.\n\n**Dependency submodule (Maintain):** Refactor all shell scripts with explicit backslash-prefixed command names to prevent alias shadowing. Add `Maintain/Pull/Dependency.sh` and `Maintain/Pull/Tauri.sh` to automate upstream merge workflows for dependency forks and Tauri ecosystem sub-dependencies. Fix escape sequence in Dependency.sh for consistency.\n\n**Element submodule (all 8 components):**\n- **Mountain** — Complete terminal state serialization/revival cycle (`SerializeTerminalState`, `ReviveTerminalProcesses`) for workbench reload persistence. Wire six new language provider registrations (inline completion, inline edit, multi-document highlight, mapped edits, document paste, document drop) targeting VS Code >=1.87 API. Implement `configuration:inspect`, `configuration:lookup`, `themes:getColorTheme` IPC handlers and unwrap `ShowOpenDialog`/`ShowSaveDialog` envelope shapes. Convert sandbox config paths from `file://` URL to OS-native form to prevent double-encoding. Stub `log:registerLogger`/`log:createLogger` to avoid boot-time crashes and register terminal show/hide gRPC handlers.\n- **Common** — Add five IPC channel definitions (`ConfigurationInspect`, `ConfigurationLookup`, `ExtensionsGetManifest`, `ExtensionsResetPinnedState`, `ThemesGetColorTheme`) via `DefineChannels!`.\n- **Cocoon** — Rebuild all 40 ESBuild bundles against refreshed RouteManifest now tracking 130 Mountain RPC methods (up from 120).\n- **Wind** — Regenerate upstream stubs and add the five new IPC channels to the Mountain-Wind boundary catalog.\n- **Air, Maintain, Rest, Sky** — Replace Unicode typographic dashes with ASCII hyphens throughout rustdoc, Mermaid diagrams, and inline comments for cross-platform rendering consistency.",
